# Hosts every box may reach: the model providers of the four tools. 'host' means port 443.
# Claude Code, from https://code.claude.com/docs/en/network-config ("Network access requirements"):
#   api.anthropic.com   "Claude API requests"
#   claude.ai           "claude.ai account authentication"
#   platform.claude.com "OAuth token exchange, refresh, and revocation also go to this host for
#                        claude.ai accounts, so both Console and claude.ai sign-ins require it"
# The telemetry hosts (the two datadog intakes) are not listed: the box's claude settings set
# CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC. statsig.anthropic.com is in no current list.
api.anthropic.com
claude.ai
platform.claude.com
# Cursor, from https://cursor.com/docs/enterprise/network-configuration (the granular list):
#   api2.cursor.sh "most API requests"; api5.cursor.sh "agent requests";
#   authenticate.cursor.sh "authorization endpoint"; prod.authentication.cursor.sh "production
#   token issuer"; authentication.cursor.sh "backend JWT issuer". It lists no CLI-only hosts.
api2.cursor.sh
api5.cursor.sh
authenticate.cursor.sh
prod.authentication.cursor.sh
authentication.cursor.sh
